At the start I want to express copious and sincere appreciation to the
spoilers authors and the other helpful denizens of this newsgroup. I
learned of NetHack only this July, and started playing real (not explore
mode) games last month. I have spent too many hours studying the
spoilers and newsgroups posts. (My news server holds a year of posts.)
Thanks to your tutelage and research, I now enter each game truly
believing it is mine to lose.

Small biographical note: for eight years I wrote for the "C/C++ Users
Journal." I have studied the NetHack source a bit. However, because of a
disabling medical condition, I am no longer a programmer or writer; and
I don't expect to use the code as a resource in understanding or
predicting game behavior. At the same time, I'm happy some of you have
contributed the Talmudic scholarship necessary to grok or even alter the
game source. We all profit from your study.

I play only vanilla NetHack 3.4.3, the Mac OS X Qt/tiles version.

